        { "text": "$\\frac{7x+10}{12}$", "correct": true },
        { "text": "$\\frac{7x+2}{12}$", "why": "Multiplied only the $x$ term of each numerator by its scaling factor." },
        { "text": "$\\frac{7x+4}{12}$", "why": "Multiplied each numerator by its own denominator instead of the other one's." },
        { "text": "$\\frac{2x+2}{12}$", "why": "Added the numerators without first rescaling them to twelfths." }
      ],
      "solution_text": "$\\frac{x+4}{3} + \\frac{x-2}{4}$\n$= \\frac{4(x+4)}{12} + \\frac{3(x-2)}{12}$\n$= \\frac{4(x+4) + 3(x-2)}{12}$\n$= \\frac{4x+16+3x-6}{12}$\n$= \\frac{7x+10}{12}$"
    },
