        { "text": "$\\frac{y+16}{12}$", "correct": true },
        { "text": "$\\frac{y-4}{12}$", "why": "Expanded $-2(y-5)$ as $-2y-10$ instead of $-2y+10$." },
        { "text": "$\\frac{y+7}{12}$", "why": "Multiplied only the $y$ term of each numerator by its scaling factor." },
        { "text": "$\\frac{7}{12}$", "why": "Subtracted the numerators without first rescaling them to twelfths." }
      ],
      "solution_text": "$\\frac{y+2}{4} - \\frac{y-5}{6}$\n$= \\frac{3(y+2)}{12} - \\frac{2(y-5)}{12}$\n$= \\frac{3(y+2) - 2(y-5)}{12}$\n$= \\frac{3y+6-2y+10}{12}$\n$= \\frac{y+16}{12}$"
    },
