      "options": [
        { "text": "$\\frac{11x-7}{12}$", "correct": true },
        { "text": "$\\frac{7x-7}{12}$", "why": "Expanded $-2(2-x)$ as $-4-2x$ instead of $-4+2x$." },
        { "text": "$\\frac{11x+1}{12}$", "why": "Expanded $-2(2-x)$ as $+4+2x$, losing the minus sign entirely." },
        { "text": "$\\frac{4x-3}{12}$", "why": "Subtracted the numerators without rescaling either fraction to twelfths." }
      ],
      "solution_text": "$\\frac{3x-1}{4} - \\frac{2-x}{6}$\n$= \\frac{3(3x-1)}{12} - \\frac{2(2-x)}{12}$\n$= \\frac{3(3x-1) - 2(2-x)}{12}$\n$= \\frac{9x-3-4+2x}{12}$\n$= \\frac{11x-7}{12}$"
    },
