      "solution_text": "$\\frac{2(m+3)}{5} - \\frac{m-4}{10}$\n$= \\frac{4(m+3)}{10} - \\frac{m-4}{10}$\n$= \\frac{4(m+3) - (m-4)}{10}$\n$= \\frac{4m+12-m+4}{10}$\n$= \\frac{3m+16}{10}$"
